Notebook[{Cell["MagneticTB", "GuideTitle"], Cell["MagneticTB constructs analytical tight-binding Hamiltonians from crystal symmetry and local orbital information. It supports ordinary space groups, magnetic space groups, and finite discrete spin-space groups.", "GuideAbstract"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Tutorials: start here", "GuideTutorialsSection"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Getting Started with MagneticTB", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MagneticTB/tutorial/GettingStarted"]}], "GuideTutorial"], Cell["Install, update, and load the package, then build a graphene Hamiltonian and plot its bands.", "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["General MagneticTB Examples", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MagneticTB/tutorial/GeneralExamples"]}], "GuideTutorial"], Cell["Follow complete model examples from symmetry operations to Hamiltonians and band structures.", "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Crystal structure, Brillouin zone, and k paths", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MagneticTB/tutorial/CrystalAndKPaths"]}], "GuideTutorial"], Cell["Draw a noncollinear magnetic Kagome structure, its Brillouin zone, and its bands.", "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Fitting MagneticTB bands to VASP", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MagneticTB/tutorial/BandFitting"]}], "GuideTutorial"], Cell["Fit VASP bands with nearest- and second-neighbor hopping, or select an energy window or k-point region.", "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["High-symmetry tetragonal antiferromagnet: spin symmetry and SOC", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MagneticTB/tutorial/ContinuousSymmetry"]}], "GuideTutorial"], Cell["Compare an antiferromagnet with SOC against the continuous spin symmetry required without SOC.", "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Band corepresentations with MSGCorep", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MagneticTB/tutorial/Corepresentations"]}], "GuideTutorial"], Cell["Load MSGCorep explicitly and calculate 